{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Moses rose up and went, etc.</b> One needs to know the reason for its saying <b>וַיָּקָם</b>, and if it is to inform us that he had been sitting, what do we gain from this information? Rather, it intends along the lines of what Scripture says (Proverbs 16:18): ״לִפְנֵי שֶׁבֶר גָּאוֹן וְלִפְנֵי כָבוֹד עֲנָוָה״, and our Sages of blessed memory said (Exodus Rabbah 45:5): I humbled myself — I was exalted. And this is the meaning of the verse ״וַיָּקָם מֹשֶׁה״ — there was an act of rising for him in that he went to Dathan and Abiram, the wicked men who had insulted him and refused to come to him, and he humbled himself and went to them. Concerning them it is said ״לִפְנֵי שֶׁבֶר גָּאוֹן״, and concerning Moses ״וְלִפְנֵי כָבוֹד עֲנָוָה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:23.360429601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}